  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ALIM COOPERATIVA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Programme will strengthen inclusive value chains that enable poor women and men to claim their rights to grow or buy sufficientfood. The Programme will support the development of the soy, boer beans and sesame value chains in the districts of Ma&#xfa;a, Metarica,Nipepe and Cuamba. Will also support the development of the honey value chain in Marrupa ensuring sustainable use o natural resource. and contributing to conservation biological and ecological diversity.    The intervention will also contribute to close the gap in the financial inclusion of the most vulnerable groups, particularly women and young people by increasing access to finance, developing business skills in mentioned district in Niassa province, through strategic partnership with ALIMI cooperative and private sector financial entities such GAPI
The program is implemented by a consortium led by Oxfam, in partnership with the Niassa Provincial Union of Peasants (UPCN), ALIMI &#x2013; Cooperative, and ROADS &#x2013; Network of Organizations for the Environment and Sustainable Development of Niassa, with financial support from the Embassy of Sweden.
The overall goal of the project is to &#x201c;Increase livelihood opportunities for people living in poverty, particularly the most vulnerable, in the districts of Nipepe, Ma&#xfa;a, Marrupa, Metarica and Cuamba&#x201d;, through delivering innovative intervention to increase production, productivity, resilience and income generation   for sustainable food security and nutrition, across three pathways of change to achieve three mutually reinforcing sub-goals such: (i) Pathway 1 - Resilient Agriculture (Sub goal): Increased agricultural production, productivity, and resilience through regenerative agriculture andsustainable agriculture practices; (ii) Pathway 2 - Food and Nutrition Security (Sub goal): Improved food and nutrition security, especially reducing malnutrition among children under 5 and women; (iii) Pathway 3 - Sustainable Income (Sub-goal): Increased income generation opportunities for vulnerable households, in particular young people and female-headed households in Nipepe, Ma&#xfa;a, Marrupa, Metarica and Cuamba district.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ALIMI is a Mozambican agricultural cooperative, based in the city of Cuamba, which produces cereals and pulses and sells them wholesale in the local markets of Lichinga, Cuamba, Guru&#xe9; District and Nampula City.ALIMI will be responsible for increasing income-generating opportunities for vulnerable, young and female-headed families.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cooperativa ALIMI</narrative>
  </participating-org>
